## 3. Page-by-Page UI/UX Structure

### A. Landing Page (`/`)
- **Hero:** White background, subtle slow-moving purple mesh-gradient blob (CSS/SVG, animated via Framer Motion `x`/`y` loop), bold Playfair headline, single primary CTA → Sign Up, secondary ghost CTA → Funding. Modeled on Cake.me's hero confidence: one headline, one sub-line, one button, no clutter.
- **Value Proposition:** 3-column responsive grid (`grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3`) — Funding / Mentorship / Networking, each a card with a Lucide icon, short label, one-line description, subtle hover lift.

### B. About Page (`/about`)
- **Hero container:** Dark theme (`bg-[#2e1065]`), white text.
  - Headline: **"Empowering Women Founders. Engineering Financial Success."** — accent word(s) in Electric Indigo.
  - Sub-headline: "We are an AI-driven ecosystem..."
- **The Ecosystem grid:** `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2`, white cards with subtle purple borders, one per module:
  - Intelligent Scheme Matcher — `<Target/>`
  - BizCalculus — `<Calculator/>`
  - Doc Whisperer — `<FileCheck/>`
  - Gamified Mentorship Hub — `<Trophy/>`
- **Tech Stack section:** Frosted glass card (`backdrop-blur-md bg-white/10 border border-white/20`) over the dark purple background, listing React, Node.js, MongoDB, FAISS with small logo chips.

### C. Core Feature Workspaces — Sidebar + Main Content Dashboard Layout
Same structural DNA across all three (consistency > novelty here):

- **Funding (`/funding`):** Left sidebar = filters (Grant/Loan, Scheme type); Main area = masonry grid of Scheme Cards (CGTMSE, Mudra, etc.) each with a prominent "Apply / Check Eligibility" button. This mirrors Cake.me's report-generation layout — filters/input on one side, results on the other.
- **Mentorship (`/mentorship`):** Top = large Mock Pitch Simulator CTA (Cake.me-style hero-inside-a-page pattern); Main area = Readiness Score Matrix (Recharts radar chart, directly inspired by Cake.me's skill-radar visualization) + list of AI/Human mentors below.
- **Networking (`/networking`):** Feed-style directory layout — search bar top, list of peer/expert cards below with `<UserPlus/>` connect buttons.

### D. Two-Panel "Input → Live Report" Pattern (Doc Whisperer / BizCalculus / Scheme Matcher)
Directly modeled on Cake.me's AI Resume Checker screen (input form left, structured animated report right):
- **Left panel:** the input mechanism (idea textarea, PDF dropzone, or business details) with a numbered step indicator (`① Upload`, `② Add context`) exactly like Cake.me's Step 1/2/3 flow.
- **Right panel:** a live-updating structured report — score ring, category breakdown bars, highlight/improvement call-out boxes — populated via Framer Motion stagger animation as sections resolve, never a blank wait state.

